{
  "id": "harnesys.webhook",
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "platform": 1,
  "title": "Webhook",
  "description": "HTTP webhook triggers for agent threads. Every webhook.http instance gets its own public endpoint with a generated token, optional HMAC or API key verification, payload-to-task text shaping (path, template, fallback), dedupe, idempotency replay, throttling, custom success responses and a delivery log.",
  "runtime": { "entry": "dist/index.js", "profile": "trusted" },
  "activation": "lazy",
  "connections": [],
  "permissions": [
    {
      "id": "trigger",
      "reason": "Fire webhook.http instances when their public endpoint is called"
    },
    {
      "id": "routes.public",
      "reason": "Expose the public POST endpoint that wakes the thread"
    }
  ],
  "data": { "migrations": "migrations", "quotaMb": 8 },
  "contributions": [
    {
      "id": "http",
      "family": "trigger",
      "descriptor": {
        "kind": "webhook.http",
        "title": "Webhook",
        "description": "Wake the thread when a public HTTP endpoint is called",
        "configFields": [
          {
            "key": "auth",
            "label": "Verification",
            "type": "select",
            "required": false,
            "default": "none",
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "none",
                "label": "None",
                "help": "Anyone with the URL can wake the thread. The URL is the secret: rotate it if it leaks."
              },
              {
                "value": "hmac",
                "label": "HMAC signature",
                "help": "Verify a signature header computed as HMAC over the exact raw request body with this webhook's secret."
              },
              {
                "value": "apiKey",
                "label": "API key header",
                "help": "Require this webhook's secret in a request header."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "signatureHeader",
            "label": "Signature header",
            "type": "text",
            "required": false,
            "default": "x-hub-signature-256",
            "help": "Header carrying the signature; an algo= prefix such as sha256= is stripped before comparison",
            "visibleWhen": { "key": "auth", "equals": "hmac" }
          },
          {
            "key": "signatureAlgo",
            "label": "Signature algorithm",
            "type": "select",
            "required": false,
            "default": "sha256",
            "options": [
              { "value": "sha256", "label": "sha256" },
              { "value": "sha1", "label": "sha1" },
              { "value": "sha512", "label": "sha512" }
            ],
            "visibleWhen": { "key": "auth", "equals": "hmac" }
          },
          {
            "key": "signatureEncoding",
            "label": "Signature encoding",
            "type": "select",
            "required": false,
            "default": "hex",
            "options": [
              { "value": "hex", "label": "hex" },
              { "value": "base64", "label": "base64" }
            ],
            "visibleWhen": { "key": "auth", "equals": "hmac" }
          },
          {
            "key": "keyHeader",
            "label": "Key header",
            "type": "text",
            "required": false,
            "default": "x-harnesys-key",
            "help": "Header that must carry the webhook secret",
            "visibleWhen": { "key": "auth", "equals": "apiKey" }
          },
          {
            "key": "payload",
            "label": "Payload",
            "type": "group",
            "required": false,
            "fields": [
              {
                "key": "textPath",
                "label": "Text path",
                "type": "text",
                "required": false,
                "placeholder": "issue.title",
                "help": "Dot path into the JSON payload used as the task text"
              },
              {
                "key": "textTemplate",
                "label": "Text template",
                "type": "textarea",
                "required": false,
                "help": "Rendered with {{text}} and {{payload}} placeholders; wins over the text path",
                "placeholder": "PR {{payload}} needs review"
              },
              {
                "key": "detail",
                "label": "Fallback payload",
                "type": "textarea",
                "required": false,
                "help": "Sent when the request carries no text"
              },
              {
                "key": "maxTextKb",
                "label": "Max text, KB",
                "type": "number",
                "required": false,
                "default": 8,
                "help": "Payload-derived task text is truncated to this size"
              },
              {
                "key": "samplePayload",
                "label": "Test payload",
                "type": "textarea",
                "required": false,
                "help": "Body used by the Send test action; parsed as JSON when possible",
                "placeholder": "{\"text\": \"hello\"}"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "noise",
            "label": "Noise control",
            "type": "group",
            "required": false,
            "advanced": true,
            "collapsible": true,
            "fields": [
              {
                "key": "dedupeWindowSec",
                "label": "Dedupe window, sec",
                "type": "number",
                "required": false,
                "default": 0,
                "help": "Identical payloads inside the window replay the previous result instead of firing again (0 disables)"
              },
              {
                "key": "throttleSec",
                "label": "Throttle, sec",
                "type": "number",
                "required": false,
                "default": 0,
                "help": "Requests closer than this to the previous fired request get 429 (0 disables)"
              },
              {
                "key": "honorIdempotencyKey",
                "label": "Honor Idempotency-Key",
                "type": "boolean",
                "required": false,
                "default": true,
                "widget": { "kind": "switch" },
                "help": "A repeated Idempotency-Key header within 24h replays the stored result instead of firing again"
              },
              {
                "key": "allowGet",
                "label": "Accept GET",
                "type": "boolean",
                "required": false,
                "default": false,
                "widget": { "kind": "switch" },
                "help": "Also fire on GET requests; the task text comes from the text query parameter"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "response",
            "label": "Response",
            "type": "group",
            "required": false,
            "advanced": true,
            "fields": [
              {
                "key": "respondMode",
                "label": "Success response",
                "type": "select",
                "required": false,
                "default": "default",
                "options": [
                  { "value": "default", "label": "Default 202" },
                  {
                    "value": "custom",
                    "label": "Custom body",
                    "help": "Return your own status and JSON body when the fire succeeds"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "key": "responseStatus",
                "label": "Response status",
                "type": "number",
                "required": false,
                "default": 200,
                "visibleWhen": { "key": "respondMode", "equals": "custom" }
              },
              {
                "key": "responseBody",
                "label": "Response body (JSON)",
                "type": "textarea",
                "required": false,
                "visibleWhen": { "key": "respondMode", "equals": "custom" },
                "help": "Returned when the fire succeeds; raw text is sent as {\"text\": ...} if it is not valid JSON"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "limits": { "throttleSec": 2, "maxBurst": 20 }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "family": "route",
      "descriptor": {
        "id": "hook",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/:token",
        "exposure": "public",
        "bodyLimitKb": 512
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hook-get",
      "family": "route",
      "descriptor": {
        "id": "hook-get",
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/:token",
        "exposure": "public",
        "bodyLimitKb": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "instances",
      "family": "route",
      "descriptor": { "id": "instances", "method": "GET", "path": "/instances", "role": "member" }
    },
    {
      "id": "deliveries",
      "family": "route",
      "descriptor": { "id": "deliveries", "method": "GET", "path": "/deliveries", "role": "member" }
    },
    {
      "id": "rotate-url",
      "family": "route",
      "descriptor": {
        "id": "rotate-url",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/rotate-url/:token",
        "role": "admin"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rotate-secret",
      "family": "route",
      "descriptor": {
        "id": "rotate-secret",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/rotate-secret/:token",
        "role": "admin"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "test",
      "family": "route",
      "descriptor": { "id": "test", "method": "POST", "path": "/test/:token", "role": "admin" }
    },
    {
      "id": "main",
      "family": "view",
      "descriptor": {
        "id": "main",
        "title": "Webhook",
        "sections": [
          { "type": "status" },
          { "type": "capabilities" },
          { "type": "permissions" },
          { "type": "automations", "triggers": ["webhook.http"] },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "title": "Webhooks",
            "source": { "route": "/instances" },
            "columns": [
              { "key": "name", "label": "Name", "format": "text" },
              { "key": "endpoint", "label": "Endpoint", "format": "copy" },
              { "key": "auth", "label": "Auth", "format": "text" },
              { "key": "status", "label": "Status", "format": "badge" },
              { "key": "lastFiredAt", "label": "Last fired", "format": "datetime" },
              { "key": "fires", "label": "Fires", "format": "number" },
              { "key": "lastError", "label": "Last error", "format": "text" }
            ],
            "rowActions": [
              {
                "id": "test",
                "label": "Send test",
                "route": { "route": "/test/:token" }
              },
              {
                "id": "rotate-url",
                "label": "Rotate URL",
                "route": { "route": "/rotate-url/:token" },
                "confirm": "Rotate this webhook URL? The old URL stops working immediately."
              },
              {
                "id": "rotate-secret",
                "label": "Rotate secret",
                "route": { "route": "/rotate-secret/:token" },
                "confirm": "Rotate this webhook secret? Senders must recompute signatures or keys with the new secret.",
                "destructive": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "title": "Recent deliveries",
            "source": { "route": "/deliveries" },
            "columns": [
              { "key": "receivedAt", "label": "Received", "format": "datetime" },
              { "key": "webhook", "label": "Webhook", "format": "text" },
              { "key": "outcome", "label": "Outcome", "format": "badge" },
              { "key": "method", "label": "Method", "format": "text" },
              { "key": "summary", "label": "Summary", "format": "text" },
              { "key": "error", "label": "Error", "format": "text" }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "markdown",
            "body": "Every webhook is a trigger instance bound to a thread and exposed on a public endpoint with a generated token: the endpoint is a secret, rotate the URL if it leaks. curl example: curl -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"text\": \"...\"}' https://<host>/addons/public/<orgId>/harnesys.webhook/r/<token> — the fast path reads the top-level .text field; use the text path or template fields for other payloads. With HMAC verification the sender signs the exact raw body and sends it in the signature header, for example X-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=<hmac-hex>, computed with the webhook secret (shown once on rotate). Noise control: a repeated Idempotency-Key header within 24h replays the stored result, identical payloads inside the dedupe window are not re-fired, and requests inside the throttle window get 429. GET fires only when enabled, with the task text in ?text=.... A busy thread reports queued-behind-active-run, a paused instance reports paused, and every request is recorded in recent deliveries."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
